IMPORT prelude

-- Tokyo Convention Act 1971 (Singapore) -- offences and other acts on board aircraft: which aircraft the Act covers and when one
-- is "in flight" (s 2), when Singapore criminal law reaches an act on board abroad and who must consent to a prosecution (s 3),
-- where an offence on board is treated as committed for extradition (s 4), the commander's, crew's, passengers' and air marshals'
-- powers to restrain, disembark and deliver, and the commander's reporting duty and offence (s 5), depositions (s 6), the
-- protection from personal liability (s 6A) and the political-offence and discrimination carve-out (s 6B).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/TCA1971.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amending Act annotated
-- in the body is 32/2018 (the Montreal Protocol amendments). The retrieval record says "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0124 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. The Act is short, so almost all of it is encoded. Not encoded: the definitions of consular officer and
-- pilot in command beyond their use here, the Minister's Gazette declarations of Convention and Protocol countries and the Article
-- 18 joint-operator notifications (s 2(4)) -- treated as given facts --, s 5(6) (air marshal measures subject to bilateral
-- agreements), s 5(11)'s list of acts of unlawful interference (taken as a given fact), the authentication and proof rules for
-- depositions (s 6(2), (3)), the consular officer's power of inquiry (s 6(4)) and regulations (s 7).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Tokyo Convention Act 1971 -- aircraft`

§§ `2(1) -- aircraft and Singapore-controlled aircraft`

-- "aircraft" means any aircraft, whether or not a Singapore-controlled aircraft, other than (a) "a military aircraft"; or (b) one
-- which "is exclusively employed in the service of the Government". (Which Government is not said; "Government" read as written.)
-- "Singapore-controlled aircraft" means an aircraft (a) "for the time being registered in Singapore"; or (b) "leased without crew to
-- a lessee whose principal place of business, or (if the lessee has no such place of business) whose permanent residence, is in
-- Singapore".
GIVEN `is military` IS A BOOLEAN, `is exclusively in Government service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an aircraft under the Act` IF
    (NOT `is military`) AND (NOT `is exclusively in Government service`)

GIVEN `registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `leased without crew` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `lessee has a principal place of business` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `lessee's principal place of business is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `lessee's permanent residence is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is Singapore-controlled` IF
        `registered in Singapore`
    OR  (    `leased without crew`
         AND (IF `lessee has a principal place of business`
              THEN `lessee's principal place of business is in Singapore`
              ELSE `lessee's permanent residence is in Singapore`))

§§ `2(2) -- in flight`

-- (a) in flight "from the time when all external doors of the aircraft are closed following embarkation for a flight until the time
-- when any such door is opened for disembarkation"; (b) after a forced landing outside Singapore, until "the competent authorities
-- ... take over responsibility"; (c) after a forced landing in Singapore, "until the time when a police officer arrives at the place
-- of landing"; and "in flight" includes any period "on the surface of the sea or land but not within the territorial limits of any
-- country". (s 2(3): territorial limits include territorial waters.)
DECLARE Moment IS ONE OF
    `boarding with the doors open`
    `doors closed and taxiing out`
    `airborne`
    `doors opened at the gate for disembarkation`
    `after a forced landing abroad, before the local authorities take over`
    `after a forced landing abroad, after the local authorities take over`
    `after a forced landing in Singapore, before a police officer arrives`
    `after a forced landing in Singapore, after a police officer arrives`
    `ditched on the high seas`

GIVEN `the moment` IS A Moment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the aircraft is in flight` IF
    CONSIDER `the moment`
    WHEN `boarding with the doors open` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `doors opened at the gate for disembarkation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `after a forced landing abroad, after the local authorities take over` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `after a forced landing in Singapore, after a police officer arrives` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 -- Singapore criminal law on board, and the Public Prosecutor's consent`

-- (1) an act or omission "on board a Singapore-controlled aircraft while in flight elsewhere than in or over Singapore" which would
-- be an offence in Singapore "shall constitute that offence". (2) the same for any other aircraft if "the aircraft subsequently lands
-- in Singapore with the person who committed the act or omission still on board". (3) not for acts "expressly or impliedly
-- authorised by or under the law in force in Singapore when taking place outside Singapore".
-- (An act in or over Singapore is an offence under the ordinary law; s 3 is not needed for it and this rule returns FALSE for it.)
GIVEN `in flight` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in or over Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `would be an offence in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `on a Singapore-controlled aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `lands in Singapore with the person on board` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `authorised by Singapore law when done outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3 makes the act an offence` IF
        `in flight`
    AND (NOT `in or over Singapore`)
    AND `would be an offence in Singapore`
    AND (NOT `authorised by Singapore law when done outside Singapore`)
    AND (`on a Singapore-controlled aircraft` OR `lands in Singapore with the person on board`)

-- (4) no proceedings for an offence on board an aircraft in flight "elsewhere than in or over Singapore" other than an offence under
-- "the Air Navigation Act 1966 or any subsidiary legislation made under that Act may be instituted in Singapore except by or with the
-- consent of the Public Prosecutor". (5) this "does not prevent the arrest, or the issue of a warrant for the arrest ... or the
-- remanding in custody or on bail".
DECLARE Step IS ONE OF
    `instituting proceedings`
    `arresting the person`
    `issuing an arrest warrant`
    `remanding in custody or on bail`

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step, `committed in flight outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `an Air Navigation Act offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the step needs the Public Prosecutor's consent` IF
        `committed in flight outside Singapore`
    AND (NOT `an Air Navigation Act offence`)
    AND CONSIDER `the step`
        WHEN `instituting proceedings` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4 -- extradition`

-- (1) an offence on board an aircraft in flight is treated as committed also within the territory of (a) "a Convention country in
-- which the aircraft is registered"; (b) "a Convention country (being also a Protocol country)" in which the crewless lessee has its
-- principal place of business (or permanent residence); or (c) "a Convention country (being also a Protocol country) in which the
-- aircraft lands, with the offender still on board". (The lessee's place of business and residence are folded into one fact here.)
GIVEN `a Convention country` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a Protocol country` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the aircraft is registered there` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the crewless lessee is based there` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the aircraft lands there with the offender on board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is treated as committed in the country` IF
        `a Convention country`
    AND (    `the aircraft is registered there`
         OR  (    `a Protocol country`
              AND (`the crewless lessee is based there` OR `the aircraft lands there with the offender on board`)))

§§ `5(2), (3) -- the commander's power to restrain, and who must help`

-- (2) if the commander "has reasonable grounds to believe" that a person (a) "has done or is about to do any act ... which jeopardises
-- or may jeopardise" (i) safety of the aircraft, persons or property, or (ii) "good order and discipline on board"; or (b) has done an
-- act "which in the opinion of the commander is a serious offence", the commander "may take ... such reasonable measures, including
-- restraint of his or her person, as may be necessary". Only while the aircraft is in flight.
GIVEN `the aircraft is in flight now` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `grounds to believe a threat to safety` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `grounds to believe a threat to good order` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `grounds to believe a serious offence was done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the commander may restrain the person` IF
        `the aircraft is in flight now`
    AND (`grounds to believe a threat to safety` OR `grounds to believe a threat to good order` OR `grounds to believe a serious offence was done`)

-- (3) the commander may "(a) require or authorise any member of the crew"; or "(b) request or authorise (but not require) any
-- passenger, or air marshal".
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `a crew member`
    `a passenger`
    `an air marshal`

GIVEN `the helper` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the commander may require help from` IF
    CONSIDER `the helper`
    WHEN `a crew member` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `5(4), (5) -- acting without the commander's authority`

-- (4) crew or passengers may, "without being authorised by the commander", take measures they have reasonable grounds to believe are
-- "immediately necessary to protect the safety of the aircraft, or of persons or property on board". (Good order alone is not
-- enough.) (5) an air marshal may do so to protect the aircraft "or of persons on board" (property is not mentioned) from "(a) any
-- act of unlawful interference; or (b) the commission of any serious offence".
GIVEN `the actor` IS A Person,
      `in flight at the time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `believes it immediately necessary for safety` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the threat is unlawful interference or a serious offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may act without the commander's authority` IF
        `in flight at the time`
    AND `believes it immediately necessary for safety`
    AND CONSIDER `the actor`
        WHEN `an air marshal` THEN `the threat is unlawful interference or a serious offence`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `5(7) -- keeping someone restrained after landing`

-- Restraint "must not be continued after the time when the aircraft first thereafter ceases to be in flight unless before or as soon
-- as is reasonably practicable after that time the commander ... causes notification ... to be sent to an appropriate authority" of
-- that country; then it may continue (a) until the first occasion the commander can, with any requisite consent, disembark or
-- deliver the person; or (b) "if the person under restraint agrees to continue his or her journey under restraint".
GIVEN `the authority was notified` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the first chance to disembark or deliver has not yet come` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person agrees to travel on under restraint` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the restraint may continue after landing` IF
        `the authority was notified`
    AND (`the first chance to disembark or deliver has not yet come` OR `the person agrees to travel on under restraint`)

§§ `5(8) -- disembarking and delivering`

-- (a) on grounds to believe a threat under (2)(a) and that it is necessary, the commander "may disembark that person in any country
-- in which that aircraft may be"; (b) on grounds to believe a serious offence under (2)(b), may "deliver" the person (i) in Singapore
-- to a police or immigration officer; or (ii) "in any other country which is a Convention country" to a corresponding officer.
GIVEN `grounds to believe a threat and that disembarking is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the commander may disembark the person here` IF
    `grounds to believe a threat and that disembarking is necessary`

GIVEN `grounds to believe a serious offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `landing in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `landing in a Convention country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the commander may deliver the person here` IF
    `grounds to believe a serious offence` AND (`landing in Singapore` OR `landing in a Convention country`)

§§ `5(9) -- the commander's duty to report, and the offence`

-- (a) a commander who disembarks a person under (8)(a) "in the case of a Singapore-controlled aircraft, in any country or, in the case
-- of any other aircraft, in Singapore, must report the fact of, and the reasons" to the local authority and to the person's
-- diplomatic or consular office. (b) a commander who intends to deliver a person in Singapore or, for a Singapore-controlled aircraft,
-- in any other Convention country, must notify "before or as soon as reasonably practicable after landing". A commander "who without
-- reasonable cause fails to comply ... shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000".
GIVEN `the aircraft is Singapore-controlled` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person is put off in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the commander must report under section 5(9)` IF
    `the aircraft is Singapore-controlled` OR `the person is put off in Singapore`

GIVEN `under a duty to report` IS A BOOLEAN, `reported` IS A BOOLEAN, `had reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the commander commits the section 5(9) offence` IF
    `under a duty to report` AND (NOT `reported`) AND (NOT `had reasonable cause`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for the section 5(9) offence` MEANS 1000

§§ `6(1) -- depositions of absent witnesses`

-- If the court "is satisfied that the person in question cannot be found in Singapore", a deposition previously made on oath is
-- admissible if made "(a) in Singapore ... before a District Judge or Magistrate; or (b) outside Singapore ... before a consular
-- officer or a judicial officer of any foreign country", in either case "in the presence or absence of the person charged".
DECLARE Taker IS ONE OF
    `a District Judge or Magistrate`
    `a consular officer of Singapore`
    `a foreign judicial officer`
    `a notary public`

GIVEN `the witness cannot be found in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `made on oath` IS A BOOLEAN, `taken before` IS A Taker, `taken in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deposition is admissible under section 6` IF
        `the witness cannot be found in Singapore`
    AND `made on oath`
    AND CONSIDER `taken before`
        WHEN `a District Judge or Magistrate` THEN `taken in Singapore`
        WHEN `a consular officer of Singapore` THEN NOT `taken in Singapore`
        WHEN `a foreign judicial officer` THEN NOT `taken in Singapore`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6A -- protection from personal liability`

-- "No liability shall lie against any of the following persons on account of any treatment undergone by a person against whom any
-- action has been taken under this Act: (a) the commander ...; (b) a member of the crew ...; (c) a passenger ...; (d) an air marshal
-- ...; (e) an owner or operator ...; (f) a person on whose behalf the flight ... was performed." No good-faith or reasonableness
-- condition is written into s 6A itself. (Ground staff are not listed.)
DECLARE Defendant IS ONE OF
    `the commander`
    `a member of the crew`
    `a fellow passenger`
    `an air marshal on board`
    `the airline as operator`
    `the charterer`
    `airport ground staff`

GIVEN `the defendant` IS A Defendant, `the treatment followed action taken under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the defendant is protected from liability` IF
        `the treatment followed action taken under the Act`
    AND CONSIDER `the defendant`
        WHEN `airport ground staff` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `6B -- political offences and discrimination`

-- "Except for the purpose of protecting the safety of an aircraft or of persons or property on board an aircraft, nothing in this Act
-- is to be interpreted as authorising or requiring any action in respect of an offence under any law of a political nature, or based
-- on discrimination on any ground such as race, religion, nationality, ethnic origin, political opinion or gender."
GIVEN `political or discriminatory` IS A BOOLEAN, `to protect safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 6B does not bar the action` IF
    (NOT `political or discriminatory`) OR `to protect safety`
